WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Flight hardware

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Ground dish, BRIC-PDFU, CARA and LEAF GBC1

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.000
A lit ground dish, the sealed dark BRIC-PDFU, the lit CARA dish on the ISS, and the LEAF growth chamber planned for the lunar surface, assumed dark while the seeds germinate.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:30.000
In the two dark habitats the seedling keeps a closed hook and pours its reserves into a long hypocotyl.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Hypocotyl at 120 h: 2.3 mm in the lit ground dish, 7.2 mm in BRIC and 7.6 mm in LEAF. In the model, light shapes the seedling far more than gravity.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Sealed versus ventilated: ethylene

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Germinating seeds release ethylene. Colours show where the embryo makes it; the chart shows how much collects in the air around the seeds.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:24.500
Peak headspace ethylene: 84 ppb in the sealed BRIC dish, 143 ppb when it is filled with exploration atmosphere, and 0.04 ppb in ventilated EMCS.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Station air: cabin ethylene

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:34.000
A taped dish exchanges air with the cabin. On Mir, the cabin air carried ethylene at 1.4 ppm, the midpoint of the range Campbell and colleagues measured.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Root at 120 h: 3.6 mm in clean air, 0.9 mm with cabin ethylene. In the model, ethylene shortens the cells the root makes.
